% 7 U.S.C. 2015(e) — us:statutes/7/2015/e
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)(B)(i)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(4)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(8)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/e.yaml".

rule student_under_age_exception_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)":
the student under age exception threshold years is 18 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_older_age_exception_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)":
the student older age exception threshold years is 50 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule snap_employment_and_training_career_technical_program_max_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)(B)(i)":
the snap employment and training career technical program max years is 4 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_minimum_employment_hours_per_week with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(4)":
the student minimum employment hours per week is 20 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_parent_young_child_age_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)(A)":
the student parent young child age threshold years is 6 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_parent_older_child_lower_age_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)(B)":
the student parent older child lower age threshold years is 5 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_parent_older_child_upper_age_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)(B)":
the student parent older child upper age threshold years is 12 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_single_parent_child_age_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(8)":
the student single parent child age threshold years is 12 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_age_exception_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)":
the student age exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person age years of the person is a number N
        and the student under age exception threshold years is a number M
        and N < M.

rule student_age_exception_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)":
the student age exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person age years of the person is a number N
        and the student older age exception threshold years is a number M
        and N >= M.

rule snap_employment_and_training_course_condition_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)(B)":
the snap employment and training course condition of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the program of study of the person is part of career and technical education
        and the program of study may be completed in years of the person is a number N
        and the snap employment and training career technical program max years is a number M
        and N <= M
        and the program of study of the person is at institution of higher education.

rule snap_employment_and_training_course_condition_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)(B)":
the snap employment and training course condition of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is program of study limited to remedial courses basic adult education literacy or english as second language.

rule student_assignment_or_placement_exception_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)":
the student assignment or placement exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person assigned to or placed in ihe through or in compliance with wioa title i program.

rule student_assignment_or_placement_exception_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)":
the student assignment or placement exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person assigned to or placed in ihe through or in compliance with snap employment and training program
        and the snap employment and training course condition of the person applies.

rule student_assignment_or_placement_exception_applies_3 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)":
the student assignment or placement exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person assigned to or placed in ihe through or in compliance with trade adjustment assistance program under 19 usc 2296.

rule student_assignment_or_placement_exception_applies_4 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(3)":
the student assignment or placement exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person assigned to or placed in ihe through or in compliance with other state or local government employment and training program
        and the person is secretary determined other state or local government employment and training program appropriate.

rule student_work_exception_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(4)":
the student work exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the employed hours per week of the person is a value V
        and the student minimum employment hours per week is a number N
        and V >= N.

rule student_work_exception_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(4)":
the student work exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person participates in state or federally financed work study program during regular school year.

rule student_parent_child_care_exception_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)":
the student parent child care exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is parent with responsibility for care of dependent child
        and the dependent child age years of the person is a number N
        and the student parent young child age threshold years is a number M
        and N < M.

rule student_parent_child_care_exception_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(5)":
the student parent child care exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is parent with responsibility for care of dependent child
        and the dependent child age years of the person is a number N
        and the student parent older child lower age threshold years is a number M
        and N > M
        and the dependent child age years of the person is a number K
        and the student parent older child upper age threshold years is a number P
        and K < P
        and the person is adequate child care not available to enable individual to attend class and satisfy paragraph 4.

rule student_single_parent_exception_applies with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(8)":
the student single parent exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is enrolled full time in institution of higher education as determined by institution
        and the person is single parent with responsibility for care of dependent child
        and the dependent child age years of the person is a number N
        and the student single parent child age threshold years is a number M
        and N < M.

rule student_exception_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the student age exception of the person applies.

rule student_exception_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is not physically or mentally fit.

rule student_exception_applies_3 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the student assignment or placement exception of the person applies.

rule student_exception_applies_4 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the student work exception of the person applies.

rule student_exception_applies_5 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the student parent child care exception of the person applies.

rule student_exception_applies_6 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person receiving benefits under state program funded under part_a title iv social security act.

rule student_exception_applies_7 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person enrolled as result of participation in work incentive program under title iv social security act or successor.

rule student_exception_applies_8 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)(1)-(8)":
the student exception of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the student single parent exception of the person applies.

rule student_ineligible_for_snap_participation with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(e)":
a person is student ineligible for snap participation if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is member of household otherwise eligible to participate under this section
        and the person is enrolled at least half time in institution of higher education
        and it is not the case that the student exception of the person applies.


% 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(C) — us:statutes/7/2015/d/2/C
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(C)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/C.yaml".

rule bona_fide_student_half_time_enrollment_exemption_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(C)":
the bona fide student half time enrollment exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is bona fide student enrolled at least half time in recognized school or training program.

rule bona_fide_student_half_time_enrollment_exemption_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(C)":
the bona fide student half time enrollment exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is bona fide student enrolled at least half time in institution of higher education.

rule higher_education_student_ineligible_for_snap_participation with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(C)":
a person is higher education student ineligible for snap participation if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is bona fide student enrolled at least half time in institution of higher education
        and the person is student ineligible for snap participation.

